[14 Regression] Wrong code at -O3 on x86_64-linux-gnu
For the following code, gcc trunk at -O3 emits wrong code.

Compiler explorer:https://godbolt.org/z/3E8xf69rP$ cat a.c
int printf(const char *, ...);
short a;
long b = 3, c;
int d(int e) {
  switch (e)
  case 111:
  case 222:
  case 44:
    return 0;
  return e;
}
int main() {
  for (; a >= 0; --a)
    if (d(c + 23) - 23)
      b = 0;
  printf("%d\n", (int)b);
}
$
